 and  you're getting an income from the  property but you're not having to go to  work for the income you've you've got  the house if you buy a house you own the  house forever so forever as long as  you've got a tenant in there you're  going to be getting an income so that's  passive income active income's very  different active income is when you've  got to go to work you've effectively got  to trade your time for money and if  you're exchanging your time for money  you'll never get rich so passive income  and how I Define Financial Freedom is my  first goal was to cover my living  expenses in passive income I thought  right right now if I've got my rent and  my food and my car and my life paid for  in passive income then I'm financially  free now the exciting thing is  all right might not be something for you  but the exciting thing for me was at the  time I'm thinking well I don't need to  actually earn any more money right now  if you're making two grand a month okay  or three grand a month rather than  thinking I need to make more money I  need to make 10 grand a month or 20  grand I need to become a millionaire  maybe you need to earn the same money or  maybe a little bit more but just a  different type of income because when I  was 21 I wasn't making a huge amount of  money I was making about six thousand  pounds a month which is a good income  and was a very good income at the time  but that money was coming in every month  from my from my rent it was passive and  it meant that I wasn't living a life of  absolute luxury but I truly believe that  the best things in life  are free they don't cost anything but  they may as well cost the Earth if you  haven't got the time to enjoy them me  right now just sitting in my garden on  the hammock enjoying the sunshine it's  not costing me any money right after  after I've finished shooting this video  I'm going to go off with my kids we're  going to go to the park with my wife and  my three kids going to the park doe